{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KKDXEJ4R1S08QDP/prj_1KP390EAC1S0WTMV/pjd_1M0B2A5Y21S03V5X/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 09 Jul 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KWP48YQ91S0FBN8?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KKDXEJ4R1S08QDP/prj_1KP390EAC1S0WTMV/pjd_1KZ68J8QJ1S07M55/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KKDXEJ4R1S08QDP/prj_1KP390EAC1S0WTMV/pjd_1KZ68HXQ41S00ADV/explanatory_note.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KKDXEJ4R1S08QDP/prj_1KP390EAC1S0WTMV/pjd_1KZ67W7MZ1S0T27F/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KKDXEJ4R1S08QDP/prj_1KP390EAC1S0WTMV/pjd_1KY0B1YH11S0CQJ3/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1KKDXEJ4R1S08QDP/prj_1KP390EAC1S0WTMV/pjd_1M0B2A5Y21S03V5X/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n1,000Y+\\nBioenergie Frauenfeld\\nBioenergie Frauenfeld\\nISSUED\\n6,065.36\\nBUFFER POOL\\n60.654\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Feb 2022 to 31 Jan 2032\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nBioenergie Frauenfeld turns forest residue into climate neutral electricity, heat and biochar carbon removal.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\nNormec Verifavia\\n->\\nProject code\\nG8SJ\\nApproval date\\n04 Aug 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nBioenergie Frauenfeld\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n09 Jul 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 6,065.36 tCO₂e removed from Bioenergie Frauenfeld on 30 Jun 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n6,065.362 t\\nSequestrations\\n6,740.516 t\\n-\\nActivities\\n675.154 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nForest Residue Wood\\tBiomass\\t04 Aug 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n04 Aug 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n04 Aug 2026\\tExplanatory Note\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n04 Aug 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n20 Jul 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n09 Jul 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 5\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n6,065.36\\nRetired\\n7.006\\nBuffer pool\\n60.654\\nCrediting period\\n01 Feb 2022 to 31 Jan 2032\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n04 Aug 2026\\t6,065.36\\t60.654\\t6,004.706\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 1% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Bioenergie Frauenfeld's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 60.654 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 60.654 certificates.\\n\\nBioenergie Frauenfeld has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"